AUTODOC mixer.doc + ridevice.doc — mixer + static device registry (Task 11).
Headers: engine/mixer/mixer.h, engine/framework/ridevice.h.
Fader law (P-17, E0 record in engine/dsp/params.c): gain = (v/127)^2.

float ri_fader_gain(uint8_t v)
  Fader 0..127 to linear gain. Result: gain.

void ri_mix_init(struct RiMixer *m, float sr)
  Init mixer (fresh handle ramps 0->target over first 64 samples).
  The live backend must keep the handle across callbacks.

int ri_mix_set_fader(struct RiMixer *m, uint32_t bus, uint8_t v)
int ri_mix_set_send(struct RiMixer *m, uint32_t bus, uint8_t v)
int ri_mix_set_mute(struct RiMixer *m, uint32_t bus, uint8_t v)
int ri_mix_set_solo(struct RiMixer *m, uint32_t bus, uint8_t v)
  Bus setters (bus 0..3). Result: 0 ok, 2 bad bus.

int ri_mix_set_master(struct RiMixer *m, uint8_t v)
  Master fader. Result: 0 ok.

int ri_mix_audible(const struct RiMixer *m, uint32_t bus)
  Audibility under mute/solo. Result: 1 audible, 0 gated.

void ri_mix_render(struct RiMixer *m, const float *bus_in[RI_MIX_NBUS],
    float *out, float *send_out, uint32_t n)
  Render n frames; overwrites out/send_out; NULL bus = silence.

void ri_devices_init(void)
  Init the static Classic registry (internal table; freeze gate untouched).

struct RIDevice *ri_device_get(uint32_t index)
  Registry lookup. Result: device or NULL.

uint32_t ri_device_count(void)
  Registry size. Result: device count.
